```
let old = std::mem::take(&mut *l.borrow_mut());
drop(old);
```
Then RefMut temporary ends at end of `let old = ...` statement, before drop(old)? In Rust, temporaries in a `let` initializer are dropped at end of the let statement, after initializer evaluation but before subsequent statements. So yes, borrow released before `drop(old)`. Let's use explicit two lines for all.

